{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794659133127,"sessionID":"ses_e25fd45d9ffevqO0j4AcG7O1MF","part":{"partID":"prt_1da051411001Fu6MH1vqdNwGaK","sessionID":"ses_e25fd45d9ffevqO0j4AcG7O1MF","messageID":"msg_1da050af600108NJE1Ns29YGbO","type":"tool","id":"9p1938wlv","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"---\ntitle: Deep Research Strategy - Mistral Vibe runtime mode and cli-opencode parity\ndescription: Session tracking for the mistral-deepseek fan-out lineage researching Mistral Vibe as a governed cli-external-orchestration runtime and its feature parity with cli-opencode.\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"mistral vibe research strategy\"\n  - \"vibe cli parity strategy\"\nimportance_tier: normal\ncontextType: planning\n---\n\n# Deep Research Strategy - Mistral Vibe Runtime Mode\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nPersistent brain for the `mistral-deepseek` fan-out lineage. Records what to investigate, what worked, what failed, and where to focus next across the eight research angles.\n\n### Usage\n\n- **Init:** created by the lineage executor before iteration 1.\n- **Per iteration:** the iteration agent reads Next Focus and writes iteration evidence; the reducer refreshes What Worked/Failed, answered questions, ruled-out directions, and Next Focus.\n- **Mutability:** analyst-owned sections stay stable; machine-owned sections are rewritten by the reducer after each iteration.\n\n---\n\n## 2. TOPIC\nMistral Vibe (vibe 3.1.2, installed) as a governed cli-external-orchestration runtime mode, and feature parity of its extensions, hooks, plugins, skills, commands and agents with cli-opencode.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\nGenerated from the reducer registry. Add external or late questions through the research inbox; direct edits are imported as compatibility input and may be replaced on the next reduce step.\n\n- [ ] How does Vibe run one task non-interactively: prompt as argument, stdin or file, which flags set model, agent profile, permissions, working directory and turn or time limits, what lands on stdout and stderr, and what are the exit codes on success, provider error, denied tool and timeout?\n- [ ] How does Vibe authenticate (browser sign-in, API key, bring-your-own key), can a dispatch pin deepseek-v4-1-flash-1017 and zai-glm-5-3-flash, how is reasoning effort set, and which usage counter does a Vibe turn draw on?\n- [ ] What does Vibe read from the working directory and from ~/.vibe/ (agents as TOML, AGENTS.md, project config), what would a repo-root .vibe/ folder contain, and which parts should be generated mirrors of .skilled/ sources?\n- [ ] For each OpenCode surface this repository uses (plugins, spec gate, dispatch preflight hooks, session-relaunch loop, goal and context bridges, slash commands, custom agents, skills, MCP and Code Mode, permissions, self-invocation guard), does Vibe have an equivalent, a partial one or none, and what porting would it take?\n- [ ] What skill format does Vibe load and from where, and how do its slash-command skills and custom subagents map onto this repository's skills, commands and agent directories?\n- [ ] What hook system does Vibe expose, at which events, can a hook block a tool call, can the eight repo guards the DeepSeek Harness plugin carries be expressed there, and what are Vibe's approval and sandbox modes?\n- [ ] What would a cli-mistral-vibe executor kind need in the deep-loop runtime: the command builder, the environment allowlist, a closed model roster, dispatch-audit recognition and stress coverage?\n- [ ] Vibe speaks the Agent Client Protocol: is ACP a better dispatch surface than a print mode for this repository, and what would it change in the fan-out?\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n\n---\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n\n- Do not implement a `cli-mistral-vibe` runtime packet, plugin, or executor; this run produces findings and a ranked build plan only.\n- Do not read, print, or persist any credential, API key, or `~/.vibe/` secret material.\n- Do not modify the researched surfaces: the installed Vibe package, `.skilled/`, `.opencode/`, or any spec outside this lineage directory.\n- Do not benchmark Mistral model quality; the question is runtime integration, not model capability.\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n- Eight angles worked (one per iteration), or convergence on newInfoRatio.\n- A live smoke dispatch is attempted at most twice in the whole lineage, and only as a one-turn `OK` request in a temp working directory.\n- Any operation that would write outside the lineage directory stops that action and is recorded as a scope violation instead.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n[None yet -- populated as iterations answer questions]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n## 7. WHAT WORKED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n## 8. WHAT FAILED\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n[Populated when an approach has been tried from multiple angles without success]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n[Approaches that were investigated and definitively eliminated]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Saturated: none yet\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n[Self-owned open questions from iteration write-back -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\nAngle 1: headless dispatch contract -- how Vibe runs one task non-interactively, its flags, stdout/stderr shape, machine-readable output and exit codes.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\n\n- Installed runtime: `vibe 3.1.2` at `/Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/bin/vibe`, a uv tool venv whose site-packages hold the Python source (`vibe/`, 517 `.py` files). `vibe-acp` and `vibe-app-server` ship beside it.\n- Captured headless contract: `research/evidence/vibe-help.txt` (version, `vibe --help`, `vibe-acp --help`, `vibe-app-server --help`).\n- Angle bank: `research-angles.md` in the parent phase packet, eight angles with per-angle questions and evidence rules.\n- Comparison target: `.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-opencode/` (SKILL.md, hard-rules.json, references, assets) and the sibling `cli-pi` packet.\n- Repo runtime surfaces: `.opencode/plugins/`, `.opencode/agents/`, `.opencode/commands/`, `.skilled/skills/`, `.skilled/agents/`.\n- Hook-parity templates named by the angle bank: `001-cli-hermes-creation/010-hermes-hook-parity`, `002-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/015-dsh-hook-parity`.\n\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\n\n- Source pointers: Vibe Python package (`vibe/cli`, `vibe/core`, `vibe/plugins`, `vibe/acp`, `vibe/permissions.py`, `vibe/agents.py`, `vibe/config_values.py`); repo `cli-opencode` packet.\n- Reuse candidates: existing `cli-opencode` hard-rules and permissions-matrix schema; the DeepSeek Harness plugin guard inventory.\n- Integration points: deep-loop executor config, fan-out command builder, dispatch audit, model roster.\n- Constraints and risks: no operator present; live dispatch limited to two smoke runs; `~/.vibe/` must never be written.\n\n---\n\n## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\n- Max iterations: 8\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05\n- Per-iteration budget: 24 tool calls, 10 minutes\n- Progressive synthesis: true\n- research.md ownership: workflow-owned canonical synthesis output\n- Lifecycle branches: `resume`, `restart` (live); `fork`, `completed-continue` (deferred)\n- Machine-owned sections: reducer controls Sections 3, 6, 7-11A\n- Canonical pause sentinel: `.deep-research-pause` in the lineage directory\n- Current generation: 1\n- Started: 2026-11-14T12:25:15Z\n","path":"specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/mistral-deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/mistral-deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/mistral-deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"---\\ntitle: Deep Research Strategy - Mistral Vibe runtime mode and cli-opencode parity\\ndescription: Session tracking for the mistral-deepseek fan-out lineage researching Mistral Vibe as a governed cli-external-orchestration runtime and its feature parity with cli-opencode.\\ntrigger_phrases:\\n  - \\\"mistral vibe research strategy\\\"\\n  - \\\"vibe cli parity strategy\\\"\\nimportance_tier: normal\\ncontextType: planning\\n---\\n\\n# Deep Research Strategy - Mistral Vibe Runtime Mode\\n\\n## 1. OVERVIEW\\n\\n### Purpose\\n\\nPersistent brain for the `mistral-deepseek` fan-out lineage. Records what to investigate, what worked, what failed, and where to focus next across the eight research angles.\\n\\n### Usage\\n\\n- **Init:** created by the lineage executor before iteration 1.\\n- **Per iteration:** the iteration agent reads Next Focus and writes iteration evidence; the reducer refreshes What Worked/Failed, answered questions, ruled-out directions, and Next Focus.\\n- **Mutability:** analyst-owned sections stay stable; machine-owned sections are rewritten by the reducer after each iteration.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. TOPIC\\nMistral Vibe (vibe 3.1.2, installed) as a governed cli-external-orchestration runtime mode, and feature parity of its extensions, hooks, plugins, skills, commands and agents with cli-opencode.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\\nGenerated from the reducer registry. Add external or late questions through the research inbox; direct edits are imported as compatibility input and may be replaced on the next reduce step.\\n\\n- [ ] How does Vibe run one task non-interactively: prompt as argument, stdin or file, which flags set model, agent profile, permissions, working directory and turn or time limits, what lands on stdout and stderr, and what are the exit codes on success, provider error, denied tool and timeout?\\n- [ ] How does Vibe authenticate (browser sign-in, API key, bring-your-own key), can a dispatch pin deepseek-v4-1-flash-1017 and zai-glm-5-3-flash, how is reasoning effort set, and which usage counter does a Vibe turn draw on?\\n- [ ] What does Vibe read from the working directory and from ~/.vibe/ (agents as TOML, AGENTS.md, project config), what would a repo-root .vibe/ folder contain, and which parts should be generated mirrors of .skilled/ sources?\\n- [ ] For each OpenCode surface this repository uses (plugins, spec gate, dispatch preflight hooks, session-relaunch loop, goal and context bridges, slash commands, custom agents, skills, MCP and Code Mode, permissions, self-invocation guard), does Vibe have an equivalent, a partial one or none, and what porting would it take?\\n- [ ] What skill format does Vibe load and from where, and how do its slash-command skills and custom subagents map onto this repository's skills, commands and agent directories?\\n- [ ] What hook system does Vibe expose, at which events, can a hook block a tool call, can the eight repo guards the DeepSeek Harness plugin carries be expressed there, and what are Vibe's approval and sandbox modes?\\n- [ ] What would a cli-mistral-vibe executor kind need in the deep-loop runtime: the command builder, the environment allowlist, a closed model roster, dispatch-audit recognition and stress coverage?\\n- [ ] Vibe speaks the Agent Client Protocol: is ACP a better dispatch surface than a print mode for this repository, and what would it change in the fan-out?\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. NON-GOALS\\n\\n- Do not implement a `cli-mistral-vibe` runtime packet, plugin, or executor; this run produces findings and a ranked build plan only.\\n- Do not read, print, or persist any credential, API key, or `~/.vibe/` secret material.\\n- Do not modify the researched surfaces: the installed Vibe package, `.skilled/`, `.opencode/`, or any spec outside this lineage directory.\\n- Do not benchmark Mistral model quality; the question is runtime integration, not model capability.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\\n\\n- Eight angles worked (one per iteration), or convergence on newInfoRatio.\\n- A live smoke dispatch is attempted at most twice in the whole lineage, and only as a one-turn `OK` request in a temp working directory.\\n- Any operation that would write outside the lineage directory stops that action and is recorded as a scope violation instead.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\\n## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\\n[None yet -- populated as iterations answer questions]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\\n## 7. WHAT WORKED\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\\n## 8. WHAT FAILED\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\\n[Populated when an approach has been tried from multiple angles without success]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\\n## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\\n[Approaches that were investigated and definitively eliminated]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\\n## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\\n- Completed pivots: 0\\n- Failed pivots: 0\\n- Audited overrides: 0\\n- Saturated: none yet\\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\\n## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\\n[Self-owned open questions from iteration write-back -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\\nAngle 1: headless dispatch contract -- how Vibe runs one task non-interactively, its flags, stdout/stderr shape, machine-readable output and exit codes.\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\\n\\n- Installed runtime: `vibe 3.1.2` at `/Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/bin/vibe`, a uv tool venv whose site-packages hold the Python source (`vibe/`, 517 `.py` files). `vibe-acp` and `vibe-app-server` ship beside it.\\n- Captured headless contract: `research/evidence/vibe-help.txt` (version, `vibe --help`, `vibe-acp --help`, `vibe-app-server --help`).\\n- Angle bank: `research-angles.md` in the parent phase packet, eight angles with per-angle questions and evidence rules.\\n- Comparison target: `.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-opencode/` (SKILL.md, hard-rules.json, references, assets) and the sibling `cli-pi` packet.\\n- Repo runtime surfaces: `.opencode/plugins/`, `.opencode/agents/`, `.opencode/commands/`, `.skilled/skills/`, `.skilled/agents/`.\\n- Hook-parity templates named by the angle bank: `001-cli-hermes-creation/010-hermes-hook-parity`, `002-cli-deepseek-harness-creation/015-dsh-hook-parity`.\\n\\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\\n\\n- Source pointers: Vibe Python package (`vibe/cli`, `vibe/core`, `vibe/plugins`, `vibe/acp`, `vibe/permissions.py`, `vibe/agents.py`, `vibe/config_values.py`); repo `cli-opencode` packet.\\n- Reuse candidates: existing `cli-opencode` hard-rules and permissions-matrix schema; the DeepSeek Harness plugin guard inventory.\\n- Integration points: deep-loop executor config, fan-out command builder, dispatch audit, model roster.\\n- Constraints and risks: no operator present; live dispatch limited to two smoke runs; `~/.vibe/` must never be written.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\\n- Max iterations: 8\\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05\\n- Per-iteration budget: 24 tool calls, 10 minutes\\n- Progressive synthesis: true\\n- research.md ownership: workflow-owned canonical synthesis output\\n- Lifecycle branches: `resume`, `restart` (live); `fork`, `completed-continue` (deferred)\\n- Machine-owned sections: reducer controls Sections 3, 6, 7-11A\\n- Canonical pause sentinel: `.deep-research-pause` in the lineage directory\\n- Current generation: 1\\n- Started: 2026-11-14T12:25:15Z\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/mistral-deepseek/deep-research-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794659128337,"end":1794659133127}}}}
