{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794659792075,"sessionID":"ses_e25fd45d9ffevqO0j4AcG7O1MF","part":{"partID":"prt_1da0f32a3001E4QNRG2NxcznMh","sessionID":"ses_e25fd45d9ffevqO0j4AcG7O1MF","messageID":"msg_1da0f2352001m17Ef4pxd5bxzk","type":"tool","id":"oh0amdat3","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/mistral-deepseek/evidence && node -e '\nconst s=require(\"./vibe-config-schema.json\").properties;\nfor (const k of [\"max_subagents\",\"max_concurrent_subagents\",\"enabled_agents\",\"installed_agents\",\"enabled_skills\",\"disabled_skills\",\"enable_subagents\"]) console.log(k, JSON.stringify(s[k]).slice(0,300));\n'; echo \"=== skill user_invocable ===\"; SP=/Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe; sed -n '70,80p' $SP/core/skills/models.py"},"output":"max_subagents {\"default\":32,\"description\":\"Maximum number of subagents that can be alive at once; a spawn beyond this fails until a subagent is stopped.\",\"minimum\":1,\"title\":\"Max Subagents\",\"type\":\"integer\"}\nmax_concurrent_subagents {\"default\":32,\"description\":\"Maximum number of subagents running a turn at the same time; spawning or messaging beyond this fails until a subagent finishes its turn.\",\"minimum\":1,\"title\":\"Max Concurrent Subagents\",\"type\":\"integer\"}\nenabled_agents {\"description\":\"An explicit list of agent names/patterns to enable. If set, only these agents will be available. Supports glob patterns (e.g., 'custom-*') and regex with 're:' prefix.\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"title\":\"Enabled Agents\",\"type\":\"array\"}\ninstalled_agents {\"description\":\"A list of opt-in builtin agent names that have been explicitly installed.\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"title\":\"Installed Agents\",\"type\":\"array\"}\nenabled_skills {\"description\":\"An explicit list of skill names/patterns to enable. If set, only these skills will be active. Supports glob patterns (e.g., 'search-*') and regex with 're:' prefix.\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"title\":\"Enabled Skills\",\"type\":\"array\"}\ndisabled_skills {\"description\":\"A list of skill names/patterns to disable. Ignored if 'enabled_skills' is set. Supports glob patterns and regex with 're:' prefix.\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"title\":\"Disabled Skills\",\"type\":\"array\"}\nenable_subagents {\"default\":true,\"description\":\"Offer the agent subagents (tools.subagent in run_typescript). Off, the agent works alone.\",\"title\":\"Enable Subagents\",\"type\":\"boolean\"}\n=== skill user_invocable ===\n        description=\"Space-delimited list of pre-approved tools (experimental).\",\n    )\n    user_invocable: bool = Field(\n        default=True,\n        validation_alias=\"user-invocable\",\n        description=(\n            \"When false, the skill is model-only: it is hidden from the slash \"\n            \"command menu and cannot be invoked by the user via /skill-name.\"\n        ),\n    )\n    disable_model_invocation: bool = Field(\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"max_subagents {\"default\":32,\"description\":\"Maximum number of subagents that can be alive at once; a spawn beyond this fails until a subagent is stopped.\",\"minimum\":1,\"title\":\"Max Subagents\",\"type\":\"integer\"}\nmax_concurrent_subagents {\"default\":32,\"description\":\"Maximum number of subagents running a turn at the same time; spawning or messaging beyond this fails until a subagent finishes its turn.\",\"minimum\":1,\"title\":\"Max Concurrent Subagents\",\"type\":\"integer\"}\nenabled_agents {\"description\":\"An explicit list of agent names/patterns to enable. If set, only these agents will be available. Supports glob patterns (e.g., 'custom-*') and regex with 're:' prefix.\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"title\":\"Enabled Agents\",\"type\":\"array\"}\ninstalled_agents {\"description\":\"A list of opt-in builtin agent names that have been explicitly installed.\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"title\":\"Installed Agents\",\"type\":\"array\"}\nenabled_skills {\"description\":\"An explicit list of skill names/patterns to enable. If set, only these skills will be active. Supports glob patterns (e.g., 'search-*') and regex with 're:' prefix.\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"title\":\"Enabled Skills\",\"type\":\"array\"}\ndisabled_skills {\"description\":\"A list of skill names/patterns to disable. Ignored if 'enabled_skills' is set. Supports glob patterns and regex with 're:' prefix.\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"title\":\"Disabled Skills\",\"type\":\"array\"}\nenable_subagents {\"default\":true,\"description\":\"Offer the agent subagents (tools.subagent in run_typescript). Off, the agent works alone.\",\"title\":\"Enable Subagents\",\"type\":\"boolean\"}\n=== skill user_invocable ===\n        description=\"Space-delimited list of pre-approved tools (experimental).\",\n    )\n    user_invocable: bool = Field(\n        default=True,\n        validation_alias=\"user-invocable\",\n        description=(\n            \"When false, the skill is model-only: it is hidden from the slash \"\n            \"command menu and cannot be invoked by the user via /skill-name.\"\n        ),\n    )\n    disable_model_invocation: bool = Field(\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/mistral-deepseek/evidence && node -e '\\nconst s=require(\\\"./vibe-config-schema.json\\\").properties;\\nfor (const k of [\\\"max_subagents\\\",\\\"max_concurrent_subagents\\\",\\\"enabled_agents\\\",\\\"installed_agents\\\",\\\"enabled_skills\\\",\\\"disabled_skills\\\",\\\"enable_subagents\\\"]) console.log(k, JSON.stringify(s[k]).slice(0,300));\\n'; echo \\\"=== skill user_invocable ===\\\"; SP=/Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe; sed -n '70,80p' $SP/core/skills/models.py\"}"},"time":{"start":1794659791523,"end":1794659792075}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794659794559,"sessionID":"ses_e25fd45d9ffevqO0j4AcG7O1MF","part":{"id":"prt_1da0f3e7f001OpC66xvCd2N13T","sessionID":"ses_e25fd45d9ffevqO0j4AcG7O1MF","messageID":"msg_1da0f2352001m17Ef4pxd5bxzk","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"9aed9198d4b60a4388bcf6c5eabf36b31ad12b61","cost":0.056796476,"tokens":{"input":187437,"output":448,"reasoning":0,"cache":{"read":3968,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794659797548,"sessionID":"ses_e25fd45d9ffevqO0j4AcG7O1MF","part":{"id":"prt_1da0f4a2c001LkC2SioHZMdfj3","sessionID":"ses_e25fd45d9ffevqO0j4AcG7O1MF","messageID":"msg_1da0f3e8a0014Y2ghqaVvJ0DeK","type":"step-start","snapshot":"9aed9198d4b60a4388bcf6c5eabf36b31ad12b61"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794659802968,"sessionID":"ses_e25fd45d9ffevqO0j4AcG7O1MF","part":{"partID":"prt_1da0f4d44001XGQJEmqs7sq9ng","sessionID":"ses_e25fd45d9ffevqO0j4AcG7O1MF","messageID":"msg_1da0f3e8a0014Y2ghqaVvJ0DeK","type":"tool","id":"9u1xnk90w","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 5: Angle 5 — skills, slash commands and subagents\n\n## Focus\n\nWhat skill format Vibe loads and from where, and how its slash-command skills and custom subagents map onto this repository's skills, commands and agent directories.\n\n## Actions Taken\n\n1. Read the skill metadata model (`core/skills/models.py`) for the frontmatter contract and the `user-invocable` / `disable-model-invocation` pair.\n2. Read the skill manager's search-path computation and claimant order (`core/skills/manager.py`).\n3. Read the `task` tool (`core/tools/builtins/task.py`) for the subagent invocation contract, allowlist and denylist.\n4. Read the subagent bounds and agent filters from the captured config schema (`max_subagents`, `max_concurrent_subagents`, `enabled_agents`, `enabled_skills`, `disabled_skills`, `enable_subagents`).\n5. Read the ACP command controller to confirm that user-invocable skills are emitted as slash commands beside the ten builtins.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. A skill is a directory holding `SKILL.md`, and its frontmatter is the Agent Skills shape: `name` (lowercase letters, digits and hyphens, ≤64 chars), `description` (≤1024), `license`, `compatibility`, `metadata`, `allowed-tools`, `user-invocable` and `disable-model-invocation`. [SOURCE: /Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/skills/models.py:33-80]\n\n2. Skill discovery order is: directories named by the `skill_paths` config list, then the project skill directories (`.vibe/skills`, `.agents/skills`), then the user directories (`$VIBE_HOME/skills`, `~/.agents/skills`), then plugin skills, then optional registry skills. The first claimant of a name wins and every later one is recorded as shadowed rather than merged. [SOURCE: /Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/skills/manager.py:225-330]\n\n3. `user-invocable` (default `true`) is exactly the switch that turns a skill into a slash command: when false the skill is model-only, hidden from the slash menu and not invocable as `/skill-name`. That is the whole mechanism behind \"slash-command skills\". [SOURCE: /Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/skills/models.py:72-78]\n\n4. `enabled_skills` and `disabled_skills` are glob-or-`re:` filters, and `enabled_skills` wins outright when set — so a governed mode can pin a closed skill roster the same way it pins a model roster. [SOURCE: specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/mistral-deepseek/evidence/vibe-config-schema.json]\n\n5. A subagent is an agent profile with `agent_type = \"subagent\"`, invoked through the `task` tool. The tool's `agent` argument defaults to `explore` and is gated by an allowlist whose default is exactly `[explore]` plus a denylist of glob patterns. [SOURCE: /Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/tools/builtins/task.py:15-35]\n\n6. Subagent concurrency is bounded by config, not by the prompt: `enable_subagents` (default true), `max_subagents` (32 alive at once) and `max_concurrent_subagents` (32 running a turn at once). A spawn past either bound fails until a slot frees. [SOURCE: specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/mistral-deepseek/evidence/vibe-config-schema.json]\n\n7. `enabled_agents` is a glob-or-`re:` allowlist over agent names, and `installed_agents` records which opt-in builtins have been installed — so an agent roster is expressible the same way a skill roster is. [SOURCE: specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/mistral-deepseek/evidence/vibe-config-schema.json]\n\n8. Mapping to this repository is therefore: `.skilled/skills/**/SKILL.md` → a `.vibe/skills/<name>` symlink farm (the `.dsh/skills` pattern); `.skilled/commands/*.md` → skills, because there is no command-file format to mirror into; and `.opencode/agents/*.md` → `.vibe/agents/*.toml`, with `agent_type = \"subagent\"` for the personas that are only ever dispatched. [INFERENCE: based on findings 1-7 and the `.dsh/SYNC.md` mirror taxonomy]\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Mirroring `.skilled/commands/` into a `.vibe/commands/` directory: no such directory is read anywhere in the discovery code, and the slash-command registry is a closed builtin set plus skills.\n- Assuming a same-name skill merges across scopes: the manager shadows the loser, so a project skill cannot extend a global one.\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- Determining whether the 32-subagent default is a hard ceiling or a soft one under load. It is a config field with a documented failure mode (\"a spawn beyond this fails\"), so the answer is \"hard until raised\", and no live multi-subagent run was in budget.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Ambiguous input: \"slash-command skills\" could mean skills invoked as commands or commands implemented as skills. They are the same thing here — `user-invocable` is the flag — so the two readings collapse.\n- Contradictory evidence: none.\n- Missing dependencies: no `.vibe/skills` farm exists, so discovery was read, not exercised. Fallback: the manager code is definitive about order and shadowing.\n- Partial success: format, discovery, invocation and bounds are confirmed; the symlink farm is designed but not built. Status `complete` for the angle.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- `/Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/skills/models.py`\n- `/Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/skills/manager.py`\n- `/Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/tools/builtins/task.py`\n- `/Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/acp/commands/controller.py`\n- `specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/mistral-deepseek/evidence/vibe-config-schema.json`\n- `.dsh/SYNC.md`\n\n## Questions Answered\n\n- What skill format does Vibe load and from where, and how do its slash-command skills and custom subagents map onto this repository's skills, commands and agent directories? — Answered.\n\n## Questions Remaining\n\n- Whether a symlinked `.vibe/skills/<name>` keeps the configured directory name in skill metadata, which matters for provenance in a generated farm.\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 1.0\n- Questions addressed: Angle 5 (skills, slash commands, subagents)\n- Questions answered: 5 of 8 strategy key questions\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: reading `manager.py`'s claimant order rather than only the model. The frontmatter tells you what a skill *is*; the claimant order tells you which one you actually get, which is the part a mirror can silently break.\n- What did not work and why: looking for a command directory. There is none, so the search produced a negative that had to be confirmed from the registry instead of from a path constant.\n- What I would do differently: treat \"no such directory\" as a first-class finding earlier. Two of this iteration's four most useful facts are absences, and absences need the same citation discipline as presences.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nAngle 6: hooks and safety — the seven hook events, whether a hook can block a tool call, whether the eight repo guards the DeepSeek Harness plugin carries can be expressed there, and Vibe's approval and sandbox modes.\n","path":"specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/mistral-deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/mistral-deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/mistral-deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Iteration 5: Angle 5 — skills, slash commands and subagents\\n\\n## Focus\\n\\nWhat skill format Vibe loads and from where, and how its slash-command skills and custom subagents map onto this repository's skills, commands and agent directories.\\n\\n## Actions Taken\\n\\n1. Read the skill metadata model (`core/skills/models.py`) for the frontmatter contract and the `user-invocable` / `disable-model-invocation` pair.\\n2. Read the skill manager's search-path computation and claimant order (`core/skills/manager.py`).\\n3. Read the `task` tool (`core/tools/builtins/task.py`) for the subagent invocation contract, allowlist and denylist.\\n4. Read the subagent bounds and agent filters from the captured config schema (`max_subagents`, `max_concurrent_subagents`, `enabled_agents`, `enabled_skills`, `disabled_skills`, `enable_subagents`).\\n5. Read the ACP command controller to confirm that user-invocable skills are emitted as slash commands beside the ten builtins.\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n1. A skill is a directory holding `SKILL.md`, and its frontmatter is the Agent Skills shape: `name` (lowercase letters, digits and hyphens, ≤64 chars), `description` (≤1024), `license`, `compatibility`, `metadata`, `allowed-tools`, `user-invocable` and `disable-model-invocation`. [SOURCE: /Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/skills/models.py:33-80]\\n\\n2. Skill discovery order is: directories named by the `skill_paths` config list, then the project skill directories (`.vibe/skills`, `.agents/skills`), then the user directories (`$VIBE_HOME/skills`, `~/.agents/skills`), then plugin skills, then optional registry skills. The first claimant of a name wins and every later one is recorded as shadowed rather than merged. [SOURCE: /Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/skills/manager.py:225-330]\\n\\n3. `user-invocable` (default `true`) is exactly the switch that turns a skill into a slash command: when false the skill is model-only, hidden from the slash menu and not invocable as `/skill-name`. That is the whole mechanism behind \\\"slash-command skills\\\". [SOURCE: /Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/skills/models.py:72-78]\\n\\n4. `enabled_skills` and `disabled_skills` are glob-or-`re:` filters, and `enabled_skills` wins outright when set — so a governed mode can pin a closed skill roster the same way it pins a model roster. [SOURCE: specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/mistral-deepseek/evidence/vibe-config-schema.json]\\n\\n5. A subagent is an agent profile with `agent_type = \\\"subagent\\\"`, invoked through the `task` tool. The tool's `agent` argument defaults to `explore` and is gated by an allowlist whose default is exactly `[explore]` plus a denylist of glob patterns. [SOURCE: /Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/tools/builtins/task.py:15-35]\\n\\n6. Subagent concurrency is bounded by config, not by the prompt: `enable_subagents` (default true), `max_subagents` (32 alive at once) and `max_concurrent_subagents` (32 running a turn at once). A spawn past either bound fails until a slot frees. [SOURCE: specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/mistral-deepseek/evidence/vibe-config-schema.json]\\n\\n7. `enabled_agents` is a glob-or-`re:` allowlist over agent names, and `installed_agents` records which opt-in builtins have been installed — so an agent roster is expressible the same way a skill roster is. [SOURCE: specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/mistral-deepseek/evidence/vibe-config-schema.json]\\n\\n8. Mapping to this repository is therefore: `.skilled/skills/**/SKILL.md` → a `.vibe/skills/<name>` symlink farm (the `.dsh/skills` pattern); `.skilled/commands/*.md` → skills, because there is no command-file format to mirror into; and `.opencode/agents/*.md` → `.vibe/agents/*.toml`, with `agent_type = \\\"subagent\\\"` for the personas that are only ever dispatched. [INFERENCE: based on findings 1-7 and the `.dsh/SYNC.md` mirror taxonomy]\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- Mirroring `.skilled/commands/` into a `.vibe/commands/` directory: no such directory is read anywhere in the discovery code, and the slash-command registry is a closed builtin set plus skills.\\n- Assuming a same-name skill merges across scopes: the manager shadows the loser, so a project skill cannot extend a global one.\\n\\n## Dead Ends\\n\\n- Determining whether the 32-subagent default is a hard ceiling or a soft one under load. It is a config field with a documented failure mode (\\\"a spawn beyond this fails\\\"), so the answer is \\\"hard until raised\\\", and no live multi-subagent run was in budget.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Ambiguous input: \\\"slash-command skills\\\" could mean skills invoked as commands or commands implemented as skills. They are the same thing here — `user-invocable` is the flag — so the two readings collapse.\\n- Contradictory evidence: none.\\n- Missing dependencies: no `.vibe/skills` farm exists, so discovery was read, not exercised. Fallback: the manager code is definitive about order and shadowing.\\n- Partial success: format, discovery, invocation and bounds are confirmed; the symlink farm is designed but not built. Status `complete` for the angle.\\n\\n## Sources Consulted\\n\\n- `/Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/skills/models.py`\\n- `/Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/skills/manager.py`\\n- `/Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/core/tools/builtins/task.py`\\n- `/Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/share/uv/tools/mistral-vibe/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vibe/acp/commands/controller.py`\\n- `specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/mistral-deepseek/evidence/vibe-config-schema.json`\\n- `.dsh/SYNC.md`\\n\\n## Questions Answered\\n\\n- What skill format does Vibe load and from where, and how do its slash-command skills and custom subagents map onto this repository's skills, commands and agent directories? — Answered.\\n\\n## Questions Remaining\\n\\n- Whether a symlinked `.vibe/skills/<name>` keeps the configured directory name in skill metadata, which matters for provenance in a generated farm.\\n\\n## Assessment\\n\\n- New information ratio: 1.0\\n- Questions addressed: Angle 5 (skills, slash commands, subagents)\\n- Questions answered: 5 of 8 strategy key questions\\n\\n## Reflection\\n\\n- What worked and why: reading `manager.py`'s claimant order rather than only the model. The frontmatter tells you what a skill *is*; the claimant order tells you which one you actually get, which is the part a mirror can silently break.\\n- What did not work and why: looking for a command directory. There is none, so the search produced a negative that had to be confirmed from the registry instead of from a path constant.\\n- What I would do differently: treat \\\"no such directory\\\" as a first-class finding earlier. Two of this iteration's four most useful facts are absences, and absences need the same citation discipline as presences.\\n\\n## Recommended Next Focus\\n\\nAngle 6: hooks and safety — the seven hook events, whether a hook can block a tool call, whether the eight repo guards the DeepSeek Harness plugin carries can be expressed there, and Vibe's approval and sandbox modes.\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/cli-external-orchestration/runtime-lifecycle/004-cli-mistral-vibe-creation/001-deep-research/research/lineages/mistral-deepseek/iterations/iteration-005.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794659798340,"end":1794659802968}}}}
