{"type":"text","timestamp":1794660303096,"sessionID":"ses_e25fd45d9ffevqO0j4AcG7O1MF","part":{"id":"prt_1da16fbad001gJ7khtqNxNXO7a","sessionID":"ses_e25fd45d9ffevqO0j4AcG7O1MF","messageID":"msg_1da16ed13001wg74k2uEWChJ8u","type":"text","text":"The lineage is complete: 8 iterations (one per research angle), 8 deltas, 8 gateway-receipted iteration records plus the run-open and synthesis-complete events, a reducer-refreshed registry (69 findings, 8/8 questions resolved, 24 ruled-out directions), a generated resource map, and the merged `research.md` with the 13-row parity table and ranked build phases.\n\n**What the research found**\n\n- **Dispatch is viable.** Vibe 3.1.2 has a closed exit-code taxonomy (0–4), a `export.json` run record written on every exit, and strict `pre_tool` hooks that can block a call. An unauthenticated live smoke confirmed the exit-1/stderr path.\n- **Parity with `cli-opencode`: 4 equivalent, 8 partial, 1 none.** Skills, custom agents, MCP and Code Mode are equivalents. Plugins, the spec gate, dispatch preflight, session relaunch, the goal and context bridges, slash commands and permissions are partial. Only the self-invocation guard has no built-in mechanism — and it is expressible as a strict `pre_tool` hook.\n- **The decisive asymmetry:** reasoning effort is a six-level ladder with **no CLI flag**; only ACP exposes it. That is why the recommendation is print mode for dispatch and ACP as an optional control channel.\n- **Two corrections landed mid-run:** the goal bridge moved from \"none\" to \"partial\" (a `session_start` hook can inject `additional_context` into the next user message), and the \"eight repo guards\" turned out to be 25 adapters over seven event classes, four of which Vibe can host.\n\n**What was not verified** — stated plainly in `research.md` §13: the success path was never exercised. There was no API key, so every authenticated claim is a source read rather than an observed run. The hook payload contract, the `--output json` schema, the `vibe` vs `vibe-rs` process name, and ACP latency remain open.\n\n**Scope:** every write landed inside `.../lineages/mistral-deepseek`. Out-of-tree changes visible in `git status` belong to the operator's pre-existing working tree and to the concurrently running `devpass-deepseek` lineage, not to this run. The one external side effect was `~/.vibe/logs`, written by the Vibe CLI's own bootstrap on two read-only invocations.\n\n**Your move:** the parent merge should lift §11's ranked build phases into `research/phase-plan.md`, which this lineage could not write because it sits outside the lineage directory.\n\nFANOUT_LINEAGE_COMPLETE:mistral-deepseek","time":{"start":1794660301741,"end":1794660303096}}}
